# ---- data (large; obtain separately, see DATA.md) ----
/data
data/
*.h5ad
*.npz
*.h5
*.tar.gz

# ---- model weights / checkpoints (large) ----
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.ckpt

# ---- per-experiment results ----
# The SUMMARY tables (1.8 MB for all 17 experiments) are TRACKED. They used to be excluded as
# "large regenerable dumps", and both halves of that were wrong: they are not large, and a
# reader cannot regenerate them, because that needs the 40 GB of processed tensors obtained
# separately (see DATA.md). Excluding them meant every results/expNN_* path cited in the
# README, in CORRECTIONS.md and in the paper resolved to nothing, so no reported number could
# be checked. That is not acceptable for a paper whose subject is unverifiable numbers.
#
# The genuinely large raw dumps stay out.
# (gitignore has no trailing comments: a '#' after a pattern becomes part of the pattern.)
# 41 MB across all experiments:
results/**/per_query_scores.csv
# 7.6 MB of HIR-Bench per-instance rows:
results/**/*method_independent*.csv
results/exp11_hir_benchmark/FULL_reproduced_*/

# ...with one deliberate exception. exp16 and exp17 read exp12's per-query scores DIRECTLY,
# and those 765 queries are the evidence for the paper's central Class-A-versus-Class-B
# contrast (+0.129 against -0.037) and for the sentinel correction in CORRECTIONS.md. Without
# this file the audit cannot be re-run. 2.1 MB.
!results/exp12_partial_observed_retrieval/per_query_scores.csv

