/.fig_rename_backup_*/

# ---- manuscript / internal writing (kept local, not for public repo) ----
paper/
docs/report_*.md
docs/project_plan_*.md

# (per-experiment results are handled at the top of this file: summaries tracked, raw dumps not)

# ---- Class C: large GDSC dose-response downloads (obtain from cancerrxgene.org, see DATA.md) ----
*.xlsx
results/_audit/
analysis/**/*.xlsx

# ---- keep curated upgrade outputs ----
!results/upgrade/
!results/upgrade/**

# ...except the superseded HIR-Bench lean run (4 MB, and its AUC is now regenerated in-tree by
# `exp11_hir_benchmark.py --skip-method-perf`, which writes results/exp11_hir_benchmark/).
results/upgrade/exp11_lean/

# ---- figures live with the manuscript (kept local), not the code repo ----
results/main_figures/

# ---- LaTeX build artifacts ----
# Regenerated by `make` in manuscript/latex on every compile. EvalShift_manuscript.bbl is
# deliberately NOT ignored: it is the one artifact a reader without bibtex still needs, and it is
# small. Everything else here is noise that made every compile show up as a dirty working tree.
*.aux
*.out
*.blg
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
